        },
        "texto": "The precise design of thus covering the face of a condemned criminal is not known, though it has been conjectured that it was intended to signify that the person condemned was not worthy again to look on the face of the king. The custom was observed in other nations as well as am…"
      },
      "c-5e34ddedffe1891f": {
        "fuente": {
          "entradaId": "freeman-398",
          "modulo": "freeman-manners-customs"
        },
        "texto": "The rising of the king in this way was an evidence to Haman of his condemnation to death; it was the royal method of expressing displeasure and vengeance. An instance is cited by Rosenmüller, from Olearius, which illustrates this Persian custom. Schah Sefi once considered himself…"
      }
    },
